From ce4a0df1af804b6b3374570cef05624cc0bcf7b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 23:46:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: pluggable S3-compatible file storage backend with local
 dev fallback

- app/core/storage.py: StorageBackend interface with LocalStorageBackend
  (original disk behavior, unchanged layout) and S3StorageBackend (boto3,
  works against AWS S3 or any S3-compatible endpoint via S3_ENDPOINT_URL)
- Selected via STORAGE_BACKEND=local|s3 env var, defaults to local
- Refactor app/routes/files.py to go through the abstraction everywhere
  (upload, download, bulk download/zip) instead of raw Path/os.path calls
- Uploads now buffer to a spooled tempfile so a rejected (oversized)
  upload never touches the storage backend at all
- Add boto3 to requirements.txt; document STORAGE_BACKEND, S3_BUCKET,
  S3_ENDPOINT_URL, S3_REGION, S3_PREFIX in .env.example
- 21 unit tests on the storage module (local roundtrip + mocked-boto3 S3)
- 4 route-level integration tests swapping in a fake no-local-path backend
  (mirrors S3's shape) to prove routes never fall back to raw disk access
- README: drop cloud storage from limitations/future-improvements

313 backend tests passing (288 existing + 25 new). Frontend build
unaffected and still clean.
